.vercel
.env*.local

# docgen/dist is NOT committed — the repo root .gitignore has a blanket `dist/`
# rule, and Vercel rebuilds the bundle on deploy via the `vercel-build` script
# (package.json -> docgen:build).
#
# Worth knowing when debugging: localDocgen.js require()s that bundle lazily, on
# the first document generation rather than at boot. A deploy where the bundle
# failed to build still starts, serves /api/health and logs "Document service:
# local" perfectly happily; the failure only appears when a client first tries
# to generate. Run `npm run docgen:build` locally before trusting a local run.

